invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_hw.c
catches: aes_equiv_test
reason: the AES=hw counter mode runs only whole passes of eight blocks, so
  the blocks of a last short pass keep their input bytes and a record
  whose whole blocks are not a multiple of eight leaves up to seven of
  them unencrypted. It is the mistake a loop over fixed-size passes
  invites. CBMC cannot read the instructions, so bin/aes_equiv_test is
  what holds it: it runs every block count from zero to three passes and
  a block against the soft cipher one block at a time. The edit sits
  outside the two architecture arms, so an ARMv8 runner and an x86-64 one
  each compile and catch it.

--- old
    while (done < blocks) {
--- new
    while (blocks - done >= GCM_HW_PASS_BLOCKS) {
